cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Broccoli in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Broccoli: GenesisL1's open-source search results clustering engine"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Decentralized Science Labs LLC"
version: "1.5.2"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GenesisL1/Broccoli"
url: "https://genesisl1.com/broccoli.html"
abstract: >-
  Broccoli is a GenesisL1 in-house open-source search results clustering
  engine. It groups search results into labelled topics in the browser with
  Lingo, Suffix Tree Clustering or bisecting k-means, and draws them as
  zoomable maps (an organic Voronoi treemap, bubbles, a radial map and a
  florets map). Search sources bring records in from any search API; PubMed,
  Europe PMC, ClinicalTrials.gov, preprints, arXiv, OpenAlex, Crossref, DOAJ,
  DataCite, INSPIRE-HEP and Wikipedia are built in, and a search page with a
  tab for each clusters up to 2,000 records with no server.
keywords:
  - search results clustering
  - Lingo
  - suffix tree clustering
  - bisecting k-means
  - PubMed
  - OpenAlex
  - arXiv
  - literature search
  - Voronoi treemap
  - topic maps
  - GenesisL1
